# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (tools/ci/sanitize.sh thread). Only third-party code whose
# ordering goes through the kernel, where TSan sees no happens-before; never masu's own.
#
# tokio's I/O driver: a ScheduledIo is written when a socket registers (RegistrationSet::allocate)
# and read by whichever worker's epoll_wait returns its token; the order is epoll_ctl before the
# event, through the kernel (masu daemon tests, #242).
race:tokio::runtime::io::driver::Driver>::turn
